// ============================================================================
//  mod_titus6.zone  -  the Titus-6, weapon 11 and the last of the port.
//
//  User request, repeatedly, most recently 2026-08-14: "all you gotta add is the
//  titus 6 from the campaign which i was inspired to add because my friend
//  synarxis has it in his mod for zombies, last weapon addition and we're done."
//
//  🛑 THIS OVERTURNS THE RECORDED "PERMANENT DROP", AND THE OLD REASON WAS WRONG
//  ON BOTH COUNTS. v1.88.0 dropped this weapon because "camo,camo_titus6 and
//  material,hud_monsoon_titus_arrow exist in no fastfile in this install".
//  Re-measured against a full index of all 191 fastfiles in zone\all:
//
//    hud_monsoon_titus_arrow   EXISTS - code_post_gfx.ff owns it. The old sweep
//                              simply missed it.
//    camo_titus6               correct, it is in no fastfile - but it does not
//                              need to be. BO2-Reimagined ships the SOURCE,
//                              camo\camo_titus6.json, and OAT compiles a
//                              weaponCamo from json. Staged at
//                              zone_assets\camo\camo_titus6.json. All six
//                              materials it references resolve (three are
//                              already in mod.ff, three from common_mp/monsoon).
//
//  🌟 AND THE FX ARE NOT A BLOCKER EITHER, WHICH IS THE PART THAT NEARLY SANK
//  THIS AGAIN. mod_wonderweapons.zone says "OAT cannot read or write
//  FxEffectDef" - true of a RAW .efx, and false of an fx asset already inside a
//  --load'ed fastfile. Proven before relying on it: mod_locations.zone declares
//  34 fx lines and all of them are present in the built mod.ff. So the three
//  Titus effects are declared here and copied out of monsoon.ff / zm_prison.ff
//  like any other asset.
//
//  Without that, the launcher mode would have fired with NO muzzle flash and NO
//  projectile trail - the exact defect the Winter's Howl was just fixed for.
//
//  WHERE EACH GROUP COMES FROM
//    xmodels / xanims / camo materials / the two Titus fx  ->  monsoon.ff
//    hud_monsoon_titus_arrow                               ->  code_post_gfx.ff
//    fx_titus_trail_bolt                                   ->  zm_prison.ff (also
//                                                              in monsoon; MotD
//                                                              already owns it)
//  Both new --loads go LAST in build_ff.bat, after the zombies commons, so
//  first-load-wins keeps every shared name on its zombies copy.
//
//  📝 NOT DECLARED, BECAUSE mod.ff ALREADY HAS THEM: the four buckshot muzzle fx
//  (fx_muz_sg_buck_flash_1p/3p, fx_zmb_muz_buck_1p/3p) that the masterkey mode
//  uses, and viewmodel_hands_no_model. Checked one by one against the asset dump.
//
//  📝 NO PACK-A-PUNCH ATTACHMENT ROW. Both upgraded defs have an EMPTY
//  `attachments` field, the same shape as mk48 / insas / crossbow, so there is
//  nothing for add_attachments() to look up and the v1.89.3 freeze cannot apply.
//
//  🛑 IT IS A DUAL-MODE WEAPON. titus6_zm (explosive dart launcher, primary) has
//  altWeapon = mk_titus6_zm (buckshot masterkey, inventoryType altmode), and the
//  upgraded pair mirrors that. All four defs plus the two dart projectiles must
//  ship or the pair cannot resolve each other.
// ============================================================================

// ---- models, animations, materials, camo and effects, derived from the six
// ---- defs by parsing every \key\value\ pair - not typed from a pattern.
xmodel,t6_wpn_projectile_titus
xmodel,t6_wpn_titus_view
