// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  🛑 v1.94.0 - THE PACK-A-PUNCH CAMO NEEDED SLOT 3 FILLING IN, AND THIS IS THE
//  SAME DEFECT THE THREE WONDER-WEAPON CAMOS HAD (fixed in v1.76.0).
//
//  User: "when i pack a punched it the pack camo was missing similar to how you
//  had to fix that for the bo1 ports".
//
//  Measured, not guessed. Across BO2-Reimagined's camo\ folder every working
//  weapon puts its mc/mtl_weapon_camo_zombies* overrides in camoMaterials[3]:
//
//      camo_xpr50   slot 3 -> mtl_weapon_camo_zombies / _1 / _2 / _3
//      camo_sig556  slot 3 -> mtl_weapon_camo_zombies
//      camo_mk48    slot 3 -> mtl_weapon_camo_zombies / _1 / _2
//
//  and each of them fills slots 0..14. camo_titus6.json shipped with overrides
//  in **slot 11 only** - the "dragon" look - and slot 3 empty, so zombies
//  Pack-a-Punch found nothing to apply.
//
//  zone_assets\camo\camo_titus6.json now carries a slot 3 built from the THREE
//  base materials already named in its own slot 11 (mtl_t6_wpn_titus,
//  mtl_t6_wpn_lmg_type95_drum, mtl_t6_attach_sniper_fastmag) mapped onto
//  mtl_weapon_camo_zombies / _1 / _2, with camo_mk48's slot-3 shaderConsts.
//  Nothing about the weapon's materials was invented - they come from the file
//  itself.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
